This file explains in detail how to calculate the piezoelectric impact on the electronic structure in quantum dots.
The whole calculation is done in THREE steps. 

STEP-1.... Calculation of the atomistic strain tensors by NEMO 3-D. Three files MUST be generated in this step: (a) 'strain' for all the atoms (b) 'strain_cation' for only cations (c) 'atom_position' file. 

STEP-2.... Once you have these three files, you are ready to run the poisson3d solver to calculate the piezoelectric potential induced in the crystal. The poisson3d solver generates many files (e.g. strain profiles, pieozoelectric charges, axes, potential profiles in 1-, 2- and 3- dimensions etc) for plotting and data analysing purposes. However, you only need a SINGLE file for the next step. The name of the file is 'potential' (without the apostrophes).

STEP-3.... Now that you have the piezoelectric potential file generated, you are ready to plug-in that file into the NEMO 3-D input deck and calculate the piezoelectricity-modified electronic structure of the crystal under study.

------------------
(NOTE: We are assuming that the executables for poisson3d and nemo3d are already built. If you want to build the poisson3d.ex yourself, please do the following, (we are assuming that you are using Lear at purdue as of August 26, 2007):

$ cd poissonNEMO3D/build
$ module load mpich64-1.2.7p1-intel/9.1.045
In the 'Makefile', please turn on the "BUILD_TYPE = intel9_64_mpi_intelfast"

On hamlet
$ cd poissonNEMO3D/build
$ module load mpich/intel/90025
In the 'Makefile', turn on the "BUILD_TYPE = intel9_32_mpi_intelfast" 
